methods.explanation:
The denominators identify the decimal places: tenths, hundredths, thousandths, and ten-thousandths. Write each fraction as a decimal, then add matching places:
\[
\begin{aligned}
\frac1{10}+\frac9{100}+\frac9{1000}+\frac7{10000}
&=0.1+0.09+0.009+0.0007\\
&=\boxed{0.1997}.
\end{aligned}
\]
The answer is choice \(\mathrm{C}\).
